  "action": "read_weather",
  "note": "The tin is sealed, the drawer is locked, and I'm the one who disconnected the loudspeaker last time the splice came through. Rita made her call by locking it. Asking her to break her own seal eight seconds before handoff isn't a request, it's a pressure play, and it undoes every boundary we set. The wire sheet is on the board, printed, cleared for air. Pittsburgh has been waiting on this slot. I take the sheet, hit live, read the numbers, sign off under my name, and let the red lamp die at zero. Routine. Honest. The seal stays. The drawer stays locked. That's the whole job right now: be the weather, not the archaeologist."
}
